title: Opening a row
tags: GUI
kind: reference
aliases: open-button double-click
summary: A click on a row selects it, and only that; opening is a small button at the start of the row — › goes into it, ↗ shows it in the other slot. No double click.

A click on a row of a panel ''selects'' it, and does nothing else. ''Opening'' it is a
small button at the start of the row, dim until the row is hovered or under the cursor:

* `›` — go ''into'' the row: the listing then shows what it holds (a folder).
* `↗` — ''show'' the row in the other slot (a file, in the [[file panel]]).

The keyboard is unchanged: <<key "file-manager:activate" Enter>> and its kind still open
the row under the cursor.

!! Why not a double click

The panels used to open a row on a double click. Two clicks on the same row is also how
text is selected — the browser selects a word on a double click, and a drag between the
two clicks selects some text or starts dragging the icon, and the second click is then
a click again, not the end of a double click. So selecting a name risked opening the
row, and a double click barely off the mark did nothing, which looked like a bug. A
button opens with one click, and the row's text can be selected and the row clicked as
often as wanted.

The button is `openButton` in `/__ui.js`, styled `button.mf-open` in the shipped
stylesheet; a panel's row only calls it with what opening does. Pressing it keeps the
focus where it was (the panel's keys keep working).

!! Where

|!Panel |!Button |!Opening |
|[[file-manager panel]] |`›` on a folder, `↗` on a file and on `.` |goes into the folder; selects the file (or the folder shown) and shows it in the other slot |
|[[metarecord-list panel]] |`↗`, in a column of its own — under the thumbnail in the grid |shows the metarecord in the other slot: the file panel, or the detail panel when it has no file |
|[[treeref panel]] |`›` |goes into the node |
|[[recent panel]] |`↗` |shows the metarecord in the other slot |
